WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.560
"Will 'Black Adam' be worth the wait for the&nbsp;
millions...and millions of The Rock's fans?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.960
Or will it be Rock Bottom? Here's the lowdown."

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.600
With a release date fast approaching, marketing&nbsp;
has been building anticipation for Dwayne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.160
"The Rock" Johnson's latest box office smash,&nbsp;
"Black Adam." As expected, the first official&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.000
trailer debuted in time to pump up audiences&nbsp;
during the latest summer Blockbuster hits.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.040
A second trailer debuted for audiences&nbsp;
at the 2022 San Diego Comic-Con.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.480
With powerful action and strikes of&nbsp;
lightning, these glimpses of "Black Adam"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.400
offered audiences some clues as to the tone&nbsp;
and direction of the feature. Most notably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.520
the latest DCEU film offers an appropriately&nbsp;
contrasting energy to the 2019 outing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.600
"Shazam!" With both titular characters&nbsp;
closely linked in the comic book lore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.320
illuminating their differences as natural enemies&nbsp;
is a strategic maneuver. The light-hearted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.480
often immature tone of "Shazam!" is in line&nbsp;
with the theme of a child-turned-superhero.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.520
"Good, yeah, good. You're&nbsp;
really on top of this stuff."

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.720
Meanwhile, the trailers for "Black&nbsp;
Adam" decisively point out that its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:00.400
headliner is 5,000 years old&nbsp;
and correspondingly grumpy.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.640
Further dissecting the trailer, audiences can&nbsp;
expect a detailed backstory of how Black Adam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:09.040
gained his powers, mixed with the struggles&nbsp;
the character faces as an immortal entity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.880
Additionally, the sneak peeks include&nbsp;
a new team of heroes for the DCEU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.680
the Justice Society of America. Included&nbsp;
in the group's ranks is character Dr. Fate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.320
as well as the first looks at Hawkman, Cyclone,&nbsp;
and Atom Smasher. How this team interacts with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.160
the leading character is certain to be a&nbsp;
driving factor of the entire film. Based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:30.320
on the source material, the inclusion of&nbsp;
Sarah Shahi as Isis may imply a romantic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.480
subplot that changes how Black Adam behaves&nbsp;
in this film and any other future projects.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:40.080
DC has been planning the character's big screen&nbsp;
breakout for a very long time. Its road to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:45.040
theatrical release has been very much of the&nbsp;
long and winding sort. That's primarily a result&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.760
of the DCEU re-evaluating the way they approach&nbsp;
their cinematic world in the wake of the colossal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:54.640
misfire that was "Justice League." It also had&nbsp;
to do with DC wanting to release "Shazam!" before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:59.280
introducing that hero's arch enemy. Finally, it&nbsp;
was also a late-in-the-game executive decision to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.520
the effect that Black Adam was a rich enough&nbsp;
character to support a solo film of his own.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:08.320
Initially, "Black Adam" was scheduled to hit&nbsp;
theaters on December 22, 2021, as something of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:13.360
a nice holiday gift for DC fans far and wide.&nbsp;
Of course, as with many other entertainment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:18.080
projects large and small, the COVID-19 pandemic&nbsp;
significantly delayed its filming schedule,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:24.000
landing it a new release date of July 29, 2022.&nbsp;
Then, the film's megastar himself announced in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.600
March that "Black Adam" was pushed back&nbsp;
amidst an overall reshuffling by Warner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.520
Bros. of its upcoming major films'&nbsp;
release dates, according to Deadline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:35.840
Currently, "Black Adam" is scheduled to&nbsp;
premiere in theaters on October 21, 2022.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:41.360
Obviously, the one and only Dwayne "The Rock"&nbsp;
Johnson will star in "Black Adam." Mr. Johnson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:45.920
has been quite vocal about wanting to play&nbsp;
the role since first circling it back in 2014.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:50.480
DC's and Warner Bros.' haphazard attempts to play&nbsp;
catch up in the universe-building approach likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.880
hindered the development of several other DC&nbsp;
properties, including Johnson's "Black Adam."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.120
Now that the DCEU has found its footing via hits&nbsp;
like "Wonder Woman," "Aquaman," and "Shazam!,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.040
Johnson will finally get to bring "Black&nbsp;
Adam" to comic-loving audiences everywhere.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:06.880
Johnson is so excited to get into character&nbsp;
that he's been teasing fans via Instagram&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:10.480
about getting into fighting shape for the&nbsp;
movie ever since his casting was announced.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.400
And yes, it appears he'll be getting even&nbsp;
more buff than usual for the project.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.000
Despite the fact the two heroes are&nbsp;
perennial rivals, it seems Warner Bros.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:22.720
has no intention of bringing Zachary Levi's&nbsp;
Billy Batson-slash-Shazam into the mix just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:27.680
yet. And Levi himself has said that the two&nbsp;
foes likely won't square off until "Shazam 3."

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:31.840
Joining Johnson is a cast that includes a mix&nbsp;
of well-known names and newcomers alike. As of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:36.640
the film's most recent casting announcement, via&nbsp;
Deadline, "Black Adam" will feature Noah Centineo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:42.080
as the heroic Atom Smasher. Pierce Brosnan will&nbsp;
play Justice Society of America member Dr. Fate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:47.440
Aldis Hodge is team leader Hawkman. Quintessa&nbsp;
Swindell is tornado-based hero Cyclone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:51.920
Sarah Shahi plays a significant comic&nbsp;
book character named Adrianna Tomaz.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:56.400
Marwan Kenzari, Bodhi Sabongui,&nbsp;
Mohammed Amer, James Cusati-Moyer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:01.120
and "Young Rock" lead Uli Latukefu will all appear&nbsp;
in capacities that have yet to be disclosed.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.440
"I'm ready. We can start&nbsp;
right now if you want to."

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.800
While we have some idea of who will&nbsp;
be appearing in the "Black Adam" movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:10.880
alongside Mr. Rock, we currently know&nbsp;
next-to-nothing about the film's plot.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:15.280
DC and Warner Bros. are remaining fiercely&nbsp;
tight-lipped about this aspect of the project.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:19.040
However, despite the fact that we don't&nbsp;
quite know exactly what Team DC has in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.800
store for the "Black Adam" movie, there's still&nbsp;
some things we can glean ahead of any official&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:26.880
story announcements. First and foremost, it's&nbsp;
worth noting that "Black Adam" will indeed be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:31.920
the character's first appearance in the DCEU. As&nbsp;
such, it's a safe bet that "Black Adam" will serve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:37.520
as an origin story of sorts. That said, Johnson&nbsp;
shared the film's opening scene during the 2021 DC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:41.600
Fandome event, and in that footage Black Adam&nbsp;
is already an established superhuman within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:45.360
the film's fictional world. So, while the&nbsp;
movie may simply begin chronologically with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:49.520
Black Adam's reawakening, as suggested by&nbsp;
this clip, it's also possible that it might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:53.600
jump back in time after its opening scene&nbsp;
to establish the character's conception.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:57.440
Per ScreenRant, Johnson himself has said that&nbsp;
he'll be playing up the antihero side of Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.040
Adam's story rather than his villainous&nbsp;
tendencies over the course of the film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:04.720
He may even be pushing the character&nbsp;
into more straight-up hero territory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:08.640
which should make for an interesting showdown&nbsp;
when he eventually meets up with Shazam.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.520
Or, dare we say, even&nbsp;
Superman — on the big screen.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:13.360
"Holy moly."

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.800
What would "The Dark Knight"&nbsp;
be without Christopher Nolan?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.080
Or would "Wonder Woman" have packed&nbsp;
the same punch without Patty Jenkins?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:24.480
It is becoming more and more relevant to have a&nbsp;
great director behind a superpowered blockbuster.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:28.160
Thankfully, "Black Adam" found its director&nbsp;
in Spanish-born Jaume Collet-Serra.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:32.480
Best known for horror films such as "Orphan"&nbsp;
or the Paris Hilton-led "House of Wax,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:37.600
the director previously worked with Dwayne Johnson&nbsp;
on the 2021 Disney feature "Jungle Cruise." In an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:42.160
interview with Deadline, Collet-Serra explained&nbsp;
how he ended up on the DC comics project,

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:45.920
"I gravitated toward the origin story&nbsp;
of this unconventional character."

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:49.200
The seasoned director further detailed&nbsp;
the morality of the subject and plot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:53.760
describing "Black Adam" as the, quote, "Dirty&nbsp;
Harry" of superheroes. That understanding of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:59.200
story clearly resonated with the star, as The Rock&nbsp;
also confirmed at CinemaCon that the 1971 Clint&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:03.200
Eastwood feature was the inspiration and, quote,&nbsp;
"north star" for the direction of "Black Adam."

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:08.080
"Black Adam" is a project that has been in&nbsp;
the works for an extremely long-time — at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:13.600
least compared to other comic book adaptations. As&nbsp;
far back as 2014, The Rock confirmed via Twitter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:18.400
that he would be taking the role of the antihero,&nbsp;
Black Adam. That same year, DC set its intentions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:23.040
of repeating Marvel's success by manufacturing&nbsp;
its own cinematic universe. And despite Dwayne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:26.720
Johnson being tied to the franchise, the&nbsp;
character unexpectedly failed to appear in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:31.040
any of the previous outings, including "Shazam!"&nbsp;
where a cameo would have made logical sense.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:36.320
The exception, of course, is his recent&nbsp;
Black Adam cameo in an animated DC film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:41.120
Released in 2022, "DC League of Super-Pets"&nbsp;
features a collection of superhero animal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:44.320
friends facing their own adventure.&nbsp;
Coincidentally, The Rock stars in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:49.040
film as Superman's lovable canine, Krypto. And&nbsp;
as the film premiered, the former wrestler was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:53.920
quick to reveal an after-credit scene featuring&nbsp;
none other than Black Adam and his own pet dog.

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:57.920
Regardless of DC's rollercoaster of success&nbsp;
at the box office, The Rock has remained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:02.480
an advocate for the "Black Adam" movie. The&nbsp;
footballer-turned-wrestler-turned-actor has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:06.960
wide-open about what draws him to the character,&nbsp;
which he surprisingly refers to as a superhero,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.680
despite Black Adam historically&nbsp;
being written as the villain.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:14.400
With Johnson's monumental success as a movie&nbsp;
star, the actor likely had his choice of comic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:19.920
book heroes to portray after 2008's "Iron Man"&nbsp;
initiated the rise of adaptations. However, he has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:25.200
chosen to champion "Black Adam" into existence. He&nbsp;
is the film's — and character's — most prominent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:29.440
advocate, going as far as to say that his&nbsp;
character has the upper hand over Superman.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:33.600
"The truth is: I was born to play Black Adam."

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:39.920
Considering the ever-growing list of canceled DCEU&nbsp;
movies, the fact that "Black Adam" is so close to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:45.040
release is a near-miracle. As criticism over the&nbsp;
Warner Bros.-backed films has been inconsistent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:48.960
the powers-that-be have dropped the&nbsp;
proverbial axe on multiple planned projects.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:53.760
This includes a Cyborg solo feature, a "Justice&nbsp;
League" sequel, and a slew of other unrealized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:58.400
movies at various points in pre-production.&nbsp;
Most recently, "Batgirl" had concluded filming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:02.720
and was all but set for release before studio&nbsp;
heads trashed the feature. Yet, "Black Adam,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:07.440
with a dark cape flapping past, has narrowly&nbsp;
skimmed through the multiple termination sprees.

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:11.840
The tumultuous road to publication didn't&nbsp;
stop once the cameras started rolling either.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:15.440
"Black Adam" faced further obstacles during&nbsp;
production that ranged from coping with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:20.480
global pandemic to overcoming troublesome scores&nbsp;
from test screenings. Worrisome test scores had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:24.640
"Black Adam" rated equal to the now-canceled&nbsp;
"Batgirl" movie. The Rock-lead feature was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:29.840
forced into reshoots with the studio unwilling&nbsp;
to scrap the reportedly $185 million project.

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:34.880
Before diving further into speculation and&nbsp;
character analysis, there are some nuts and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:39.520
bolts about the film worth covering. Officially,&nbsp;
the movie has not announced a runtime; however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:44.000
a parents guide from Filmy Rating has the&nbsp;
movie clocked in at 1 hour and 48 minutes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:48.560
Based on previous DCEU films, the&nbsp;
108-minute watch seems a little short,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:53.040
with "Shazam!" clocking it at 132 minutes,&nbsp;
and the longest movie in the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:58.960
"Zack Snyder's Justice League," lands at an&nbsp;
astounding 242 minutes. Yet, 2020's "Harley Quinn:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:03.840
Birds of Prey" finished at 109 minutes, making&nbsp;
a shorter "Black Adam" film a real possibility.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:08.160
Equally, "Black Adam" has not yet received&nbsp;
an official rating from the Motion Picture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:13.440
Association of America. However, there is much&nbsp;
less need for speculation. According to Dwayne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:17.360
Johnson's production company, Seven Bucks,&nbsp;
"Black Adam" was filmed intentionally aiming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:22.720
for a PG-13 rating. Despite the rise of R-rated&nbsp;
comic book films, the story of the antihero did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:27.040
not call for the additional profanities seen&nbsp;
in movies like "The Suicide Squad." But there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:31.360
is reason to believe that "Black Adam" will&nbsp;
lean towards the harder end of the PG-13 rating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:35.840
as the intense violence and visuals showcased&nbsp;
in the trailers suggest a darker DCEU movie.

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:40.960
Although he often crosses paths with Shazam's&nbsp;
Captain Marvel and shares the same lightning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:45.760
bolt across his chest, Black Adam's powers differ&nbsp;
from his red-suited nemesis. Most prominently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:51.040
Captain Marvel — the DC version — gains his powers&nbsp;
by calling out an acronym of six Greek gods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:55.680
while Black Adam, who also yells "SHAZAM," is&nbsp;
bestowed his abilities by Egyptian gods. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.680 --> 00:10:00.480
stamina of Shu offers Black Adam endurance and&nbsp;
sustenance, meaning he can live without food,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:05.120
water, or air. The god Horus gifts him&nbsp;
superhuman speed and flight. Strength equal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:10.480
to that of Superman comes from Amon. Meanwhile,&nbsp;
the wisdom of Zehuti and the power of Aten make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:14.560
Black Adam not only super-intelligent but&nbsp;
able to use magic — an ability that often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:18.560
gives him the upper hand. And finally, the&nbsp;
courage of Mehen makes him invulnerable.

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:23.200
Needless to say, Black Adam is a powerhouse of&nbsp;
super abilities equal to — and often surpassing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:27.680
— the strongest we have seen, like Superman&nbsp;
and Captain Marvel. However, the character is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:32.320
not without his limits. Most interestingly,&nbsp;
yet inconsistently explored in the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:37.680
the 5000-year-old Adam is stuck in his powerful&nbsp;
form. Unlike the hero of "Shazam!," Black Adam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:42.800
can't transform back and forth between superhero&nbsp;
and child by saying one word. If he were to revert&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:47.440
to his original self, his body would disintegrate,&nbsp;
aging the thousands of years that have passed.

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:53.520
As a character, Black Adam has been around since&nbsp;
1945, when Fawcett Comics still published Captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:57.680
Marvel and the rest of the Shazam family,&nbsp;
long before their rights were sold to DC.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:01.920
His true name is Teth-Adam, and he was bestowed&nbsp;
powers by the same wizard that appears in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:06.240
"Shazam!" movie. However, instead of using&nbsp;
his powerful abilities to protect the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:10.480
Adam decided that he should be its ruler and&nbsp;
assumed the throne of Egypt. Betrayed, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:15.040
wizard banished the errant champion to the most&nbsp;
distant star in the universe. Taking thousands of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:19.520
years to return to Earth, Black Adam arrives&nbsp;
to find a new champion has taken his place.

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:23.520
Surprisingly, the Shazam villain only appeared&nbsp;
the once under the original publisher.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:28.400
It was not until DC owned the rights that&nbsp;
Black Adam would return in 1975. Since then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:32.720
the character has been prominently utilized&nbsp;
as a villain to DC's most powerful heroes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:36.400
including Captain Marvel, Superman,&nbsp;
and the Justice League. At times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:40.560
Black Adam has reformed, becoming a hero,&nbsp;
but he is often portrayed as an antihero,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:43.920
defending his own beliefs of what is&nbsp;
good and protecting his home of Khandaq.

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:49.040
A significant inclusion in the upcoming "Black&nbsp;
Adam" movie is the cinematic introduction of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:54.080
the Justice Society of America. As much as this&nbsp;
collective of superheroes seems like a derivative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:59.360
of Justice League, the JSA predates the latter&nbsp;
by two decades. The original concept behind the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:03.600
Golden Age team was to combine characters&nbsp;
from two sister companies into one series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:09.200
All-Star Comics. The blended stories included&nbsp;
members from both DC Comics and All-American&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:13.840
Comics until 1946, when the characters&nbsp;
were amalgamated under one publisher title.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:19.920
DC Comics later rectified the inconsistent&nbsp;
storylines in the 1985 limited series "Crisis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:25.120
on Infinite Earths," canonically making the&nbsp;
JSA a defunct World War II-era super team.

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:29.520
The earliest members of the JSA included&nbsp;
characters that have now become extremely popular,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:33.920
including Green Lantern and Flash. However,&nbsp;
much of the initial lineup remains intact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:37.760
for the upcoming "Black Adam" film —&nbsp;
specifically Doctor Fate and Hawkman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:41.200
while Atom Smasher is a descendant of&nbsp;
the original Atom. Throughout the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:45.200
there have been new iterations of the JSA&nbsp;
introducing new members along the way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:49.360
Meanwhile, the team has appeared on multiple&nbsp;
DC television shows, including "Smallville,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:53.280
"Legends of Tomorrow," and "Stargirl." And&nbsp;
depending on the reception of "Black Adam,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:57.840
Warner Bros. is receptive to the idea of creating&nbsp;
a spin-off movie for the unique team of heroes.

00:12:58.640 --> 00:12:59.520
"Make this one count."

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:05.920
The DCEU timeline is loose, potentially broken,&nbsp;
and not nearly as streamlined as the Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:10.720
Cinematic Universe. The pair of "Wonder Woman"&nbsp;
movies fill points in a timeline that seemingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:16.240
centers around the 2017 "Justice League" feature.&nbsp;
However, the inconsistent double header of 2016's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:20.320
"Suicide Squad" and James Gunn's "The Suicide&nbsp;
Squad," mixed with differently aged actors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:25.520
portraying Batman, convolute a cinematic universe.&nbsp;
A universe that is about to get even messier with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:29.680
an upcoming "The Flash" movie that reportedly&nbsp;
involves significant time travel. The whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:34.560
order of things is difficult enough to keep sorted&nbsp;
without including another time-spanning character.

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:39.280
So, where does "Black Adam" fit into the&nbsp;
DCEU timeline that is otherwise fractured?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:42.800
As seen in the released trailers, the&nbsp;
story begins thousands of years ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:46.560
making it simple to choose an awakening point&nbsp;
to align with certain characters and events.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:51.280
With news that Viola Davis's Amanda Waller&nbsp;
character from "The Suicide Squad" is set to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:55.280
appear in "Black Adam," the story will likely&nbsp;
take place in the modern day after the events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.280 --> 00:14:00.000
of "Justice League." The choice to bring Black&nbsp;
Adam into the DCEU as it currently stands would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.560
simplify any future throwdowns with established&nbsp;
characters such as Superman and Shazam.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:08.960
However, an explanation will be necessary for&nbsp;
why the Justice Society of America is reacting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:12.560
to the film's events instead of characters&nbsp;
that previously existed in the universe.

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:17.200
As a wrestler, one of Dwayne&nbsp;
Johnson's most famous lines goes,

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:19.200
"Can you smell what The Rock is cooking?"

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:24.880
The phrase holds some depth nowadays as the a-list&nbsp;
movie star is intentionally stirring the DCEU pot.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:28.400
Johnson is putting much stock in his new&nbsp;
superpowered character to pave the way for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:34.080
a revived DC cinematic collection. During his&nbsp;
arrival at the 2022 San Diego Comic-Con event,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:36.320
a large screen behind him boldly stated,

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:38.960
"The DC Universe will never be the same."

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:42.960
During the Hall H trailer premiere, The&nbsp;
Rock doubled down on the statement, saying,

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:47.520
"The idea [behind the film] was: How can we create&nbsp;
something that’s fresh, unique, maybe show and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:52.240
create things that have never been done? [...]&nbsp;
Maybe we can issue a new era in the DC Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:56.560
maybe it’s time for a shift, get in there and&nbsp;
disrupt a little bit and listen to the fans."

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:01.440
Given the unstoppable popularity of superhero&nbsp;
films and the universal approval of Dwayne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:06.000
Johnson's electric charm, it seems natural&nbsp;
for DC to want to sign the former wrestler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:10.400
up for a trilogy of movies. Truthfully, they&nbsp;
hit the lottery when the big-name star found a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:14.320
character he resonated with so deeply within&nbsp;
their roster instead of the competitors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:18.640
Unfortunately, DC projects are on shaky&nbsp;
ground at Warner Bros. Studios. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:22.720
the future of Dwayne Johnson's character in&nbsp;
the DCEU highly depends on the reception of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:27.920
his inaugural outing. Producer for Johnson's&nbsp;
Seven Bucks Productions company, Hiram Garcia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:30.480
spoke about the potential&nbsp;
follow-up with Collider, saying,

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:36.106
"We have big plans, obviously, for the DC&nbsp;
Universe, if the fans perceive the way we want."

